{
 "about": "Clips beyond walk, run and the idles. dropped: clips in anims.glb the labs leave out and the next anims build skips (idle_2 was the Stretch again: the owner, 2026-10-25). meshy: a Meshy library action, fetched on the scout donor's rig by tools/meshy.py anims (donors/anims/actions*.glb). ual: '<file>:<clip>' from Quaternius's Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0, donors/anims/UAL*.glb). make_pieces.write_anims retargets both. loop: false plays once and returns to the idle. The libraries have no hoeing, hammering, pickaxe or straight thrusting clip, so some are made (derive, make_pieces.derived_clips): loop_of a one-shot that eases back to its first frame after its last; dig, both hands on a pickaxe or hoe swung over the shoulder and down in front (dig_loop: the heavy swing looped had the left arm across the chest); hammer, a procedural loop on the standing idle (hammer_loop); thrust, a straight thrust from the combat stance, one-handed or a spear underhand (thrust_clip: Meshy's 'Thrust Slash' stabbed overhand, the point up); carry, an entry's own Meshy action ('<key>@src') with the arms holding a spear at the thrust's guard (spear_carry: 'Spear Walk' held it behind the back); hands, a clip (an idle's key, or '<key>@src') with a hand put where it only gestures, the head, the belly or the chest (hands_clip: the confused scratch scratched the air over the crown, the sleeper held both hands up), standing where its source stood. From the owner's review of 2026-11-26: level, an arm's swing flattened toward a level plane in spans (R: [its elevation from the shoulder, degrees; the share of the clip's offset kept]: slash_left from slash_up, which rose from below the right hip to over the left shoulder); bend, the spine bent forward joint by joint (walk_shoot from walk_shoot_high, which aims 13 degrees up); force, a clip re-timed by stretches (pace: [from second, factor]) and leant into its blow (axe_spin); guard, the right hand's grip put before the face with the blade across it in spans (block, block_2: the blade pointed back past the head); door, a door pulled open by its lever handle (open_door: the hand only held still in front); bench, crafting at a bench on the standing idle (craft_bench); place, a hand held at a point from the hips in spans (pick_fruit: the basket under the falling fruit); handles, both hands on a cart's crossbar at a fixed height (push). A clip made from '<key>@src' stands where its source stood, one made from another clip right after it. hold: per hand (R, L), the props (data/props.json) the clip may hold, the default first. two_hands: the held props the left hand also grips in this clip (data/props.json support). face: a hand brought to the face (KCharFigure toFace): hand R or L, at a point of data/clips.json faces (mouth, sip, anchor), point the hand's point (its grip frame) that goes there; when: spans of clip seconds it does so in (eased over ease; a span at a loop's start or end runs on round it), else only as near as the clip brings it (near: full within near[0] m, none beyond near[1]); level: the most degrees a bow's arrow may point up. nock: spans of clip seconds a bow's arrow is on the string (nocked to loosed). lead_left: a two-handed prop with a one-point support is held the other way round (the left hand above the right). clear_jaw: the two-handed hold's support arm is kept out of the jaw and the skull (the hands come down, then the elbow swings: Chop's top held the left arm across the chin).",
